# desk-nest's fixtures: <panel> <name> [place|inside] [description]
# The first line of a panel is its default. A name is written to
# $NEST_STATE/control/<panel> and read by that panel's fake (nest/fakes).
# place:  data the shell reads itself; after writing control/<panel>, the
#         launcher runs `nest-place <panel> <name>` on the host.
# inside: an action, not a state; the launcher runs `nest-notify <name>`
#         (notifications) or `nest-services act <panel> <name>` (a demo
#         stand-in's) inside the nest. Not run at start.
# Names after a weather fixture name joined by + replay one after another.
# demo-* fixtures are nest's own (nest/fixtures/<panel>/), invented data for
# Wednesday 25 November 2026 09:41, moved to now like the others.

